WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.470 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hi my name is gordon bass and i'm a  writer and i want to tell you a story  about a man  his name has been carlin  and he drove the oceans of the world in  an amphibious vehicle there was only one  problem the vehicle tended to sink  [Music]  ben carlin met my grandfather in 1947 so  i grew up hearing stories about ben  eventually i became so obsessed with his  adventure that i ended up writing a book  about him ben was born in western  australia he was a smart kid but he  could never shake the feeling that he  had grown up on the very edge of the  world and so as soon as he was able he  wanted to set off and find adventure he  started by mining for gold in western  australia didn't do very well at that  he joined the army and signed up for  bomb disposal in world war ii but he  ended up repairing latrines and runways  so he felt he'd been a failure at that  and finally at the age of 35 he decided  he had one more shot to accomplish  something that would put his name on the  map he decided he was going to circle  the world in an amphibious vehicle  the vehicle in question was an  amphibious version of the world war ii  army jeep so picture an army jeep with a  boat shell around it and that's what it  was  ben found one for 901 and spent the next  year preparing for his journey  he called it the half safe it was  supposed to be good on land and water  but in reality it turned out not to be  so great on either one  in 1948 carlin and his american wife  eleanor set off from halifax nova scotia  the journey was not smooth the entire  cabin was just five feet wide so the  only way to sleep was to curl up on the  back bench seat  the engine was so loud that they just  stopped trying to talk to each other  they hit a gale in the middle of the  atlantic they thought they were going to  die and at that point they realized they  hadn't even packed life jackets  so by the time they got to england they  had to completely rebuild the half safe  they had less than a hundred dollars to  their name so they ended up stopping for  four years eleanor got job and ben spent  a lot of time preparing the next leg of  the journey in 1955 ben and eleanor set  off they thought it would take a year at  most and they would be able to return to  their normal lives have kids and start a  family  when they hit the middle east and they  were driving through syria and iraq then  discovered that he hadn't ventilated the  jeep properly it rose to 170 degrees and  they ended up driving by night and then  sleeping in the shade of the jeep by day  so they could avoid the heat of the sun  there were bandits  and there were some roads that they were  crossing that hadn't been traversed by  vehicles since the middle of world war  ii which was ten years earlier by  calcutta the marriage was over eleanor  had enough and she left  ben continued alone oversea and land for  the rest of the journey when he got to  the states he'd hoped for a movie deal  about his adventure but it never  materialized  in the end on may 13 1958  ben completed the journey he traveled 40  000 miles over land and 10 000 miles  over water  part of the reason that ben never found  lasting fame was that there was no  deeper reason for the journey other than  to prove he could do it  [Music]  this was the era before gps and before  satellite radio and before distress  beacons  so ben was really navigating just by the  stars and he taught himself how to  navigate out of a book that he bought in  a secondhand bookstore  what been accomplished  going around the world in an amphibious  vehicle it set a record that stood for  60 years and not only has the record  stood for 60 years but nobody's even  tried to replicate it which gives you a  sense of the magnitude  [Music]  [Applause]  you

